  "id": "COMPOUND:15444 - PROTEIN:5867",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Abrotanifolon may interact with HaCaT cells, through a series of molecular targets. Abrotanifolon is implicated in targeting VMRC-LCP, a protein that is also a target of Ginsenoside R10 and Neridienone A. These compounds are known to modulate cellular processes, and their shared target VMRC-LCP may be a key mediator of their effects on HaCaT cells. The final scores for all three paths are consistent, indicating a plausible and well-supported relationship between Abrotanifolon and HaCaT. The mechanism likely involves VMRC-LCP as a central node, where Abrotanifolon, Ginsenoside R10, and Neridienone A may exert their effects through similar or distinct pathways. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
